Error result first; an errors.Is guard replaces the engine's sentinel by the repo's re-exported alias.
Expect 2 entries: sentinel repo.ErrNotFound (the guarded return) and sentinel engine.ErrClosed (`return err, v`); no kverr.ErrNotFound entry.
ErrClosed is reassigned in the engine's func init() and therefore unstable for errtrace: it carries a conservative 'possibly handled' note
(may be the same value as kverr.ErrNotFound). At run time both stores are distinct errors.New values, so the note is imprecise but allowed by P07.
-- args --
repo/repo.go:@lookup
